  "title": "FA-HUM 19 Dominican Republic simulated flood evacuaction and rescue in Bajo Yuna area.",
  "description": "FA-HUM 19 is a U.S. Army South-sponsored foreign humanitarian assistance and disaster relief exercise designed to build U.S. partner nation’s capacity for civil and military response to major disasters. More than 100 national experts from over 13 Latin American countries will operate jointly throughout FA-HUM 19 simulations and training events from May 6 - 17, 2019 in the Dominican Republic. Rescue teams from the participating Latin American countries simulated an evacuation along with a water and air rescue in Bajo Yuna area of the Dominican Republic May 08, 2019. (U.S. Army video by Sgt. Daryl Bradford)",
